@prefix : <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/vbo-subset#> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@base <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/vbo-subset> .

<http://mee.foundation/ontologies/vbo-subset> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/vbo-subset/2.0.0> ;
    dc:date "2026-08-29"^^xsd:date ;
    owl:versionInfo "Version 2.0.0 - expanded from a 4-class illustrative stub to a full extraction of every VBO breed under the 9 companion-pet species this project's example data can name (dog, cat, rabbit, guinea pig, golden hamster, goldfish, zebrafish, zebra finch, Japanese rice fish): 2,822 real classes, preserving VBO's own subClassOf breed tree."@en ;
    rdfs:label "VBO Companion-Pet-Species Breed Extraction"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A real extraction of VBO (the Vertebrate Breed Ontology,
                    https://github.com/monarch-initiative/vertebrate-breed-ontology, OBO Foundry PURL
                    http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/vbo.owl, release v2026-04-15), downloaded and filtered
                    directly from its own vbo-base.obo release artifact (2026-08-29), NOT a hand-picked
                    illustrative stub. VBO's full release is 19,961 classes across 49 species — but ~78%
                    of that (Cattle 4,199, Sheep 3,097, Chicken 2,766, Horse 2,031, Pig 1,473, Goat 1,469,
                    plus Ass/Buffalo/Turkey/Dromedary/Pigeon/Deer/Guinea fowl/Quail/Muscovy duck/Ostrich/
                    Bactrian camel/Alpaca/Llama/Pheasant/Partridge/Emu/American Bison/Guanaco/Cassowary/
                    Nandu/Duck/Swallow) is livestock, poultry, or game species with no place in a *Pets*
                    ontology at all. This file instead keeps every real breed class under the 9 species
                    this project's pets:hasSpecies design actually names as companion pets — Dog (1,576
                    upstream, 1,537 kept after dropping obsolete terms), Rabbit (914), Cat (312, 303 kept),
                    Guinea pig (25), Japanese rice fish/medaka (10), Golden hamster (4), Zebrafish (3),
                    Zebra finch (1) — plus each species' own top-level "‹Species› breed" grouping class
                    (e.g. obo:VBO_0400024 "Dog breed"), 2,822 classes in total. Each class carries its real
                    upstream label and, where VBO provides one, its real upstream definition, cited rather
                    than invented. VBO's own subClassOf breed tree is preserved (species-group → breed →
                    sub-breed/variety, e.g. "Dog breed" → "Chihuahua" → "Chihuahua, Long-Haired") down to
                    each species' own top-level breed-group node, whose further upward chain to VBO's
                    generic "Mammalian breed"/"Vertebrate breed" root nodes is deliberately NOT re-asserted
                    here (the same "omit the chain past what's actually needed" precedent
                    project_files/dron-upper.ttl already establishes for BFO) — those two root nodes carry
                    no species-specific information relevant to this file's scope. Each species' own
                    top-level breed-group node is instead linked directly to the real NCBITaxon species IRI
                    this project already vendors in project_files/ncbitaxon-subset.ttl for the same species
                    (e.g. "Cat breed" rdfs:subClassOf obo:NCBITaxon_9685) — a genuine cross-vendor-file link
                    between the species picker and the breed picker, both imported together by
                    other/pets.ttl. Deliberately excludes VBO's "Rainbow trout" and "Western clawed frog"
                    breed entries (1 real breed each) as lab-strain/aquaculture designations rather than
                    genuine companion-pet breeds. Licensed CC-BY 4.0 — this comment block, and the
                    class-level rdfs:comments below (where VBO provides a real definition), serve as
                    attribution to the Monarch Initiative's Vertebrate Breed Ontology."""@en .

